#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1124 expect=violation domain=CM
#note "column-absent case on the INTERVENTIONS arm: CMSTAT='NOT DONE' and the dataset carries no CMREASND column at all. Since 2026-09-11 the rule gates on Requirements.Variables.All [--STAT, --REASND] (R-4.11b, verdict 2-1, T1-11), so the run is an auditable SKIP naming the missing column instead of one finding per NOT DONE row. The absence itself is reported ONCE by the minted sister FDA-SD9726, whose violation scenario carries this shape. Before the gate, the bare empty(--REASND) leaf was TRUE on every row (absent = all-missing, EC-43)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset CM class=INTERVENTIONS label="Concomitant Medications"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col CMSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col CMTRT   type=Char label="Reported Name of Drug, Med, or Therapy"
col CMSTAT  type=Char label="Completion Status"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | CM | 01-701-1015 | 1 |         | NOT DONE
CDISCPILOT01 | CM | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ASPIRIN |
